# Trusty TEE
#

config TRUSTY
	tristate "Trusty TEE support"
	depends on TEE
	depends on ARM || ARM64
	depends on HAVE_ARM_SMCCC
	help
	  Trusty is a secure OS that runs in the ARM TrustZone secure world,
	  reached from the normal world through SMC calls.  This is the core
	  driver: it owns the SMC interface and exposes the fast- and
	  standard-call primitives the rest of the Trusty stack builds on.

	  Say Y here if your platform ships the Trusty secure OS and you need
	  the kernel to talk to it (for example to reach a Trusty-hosted
	  security service).  If unsure, say N.
